
Complete the migration of the existing
PropertiesManager to the hierarchical
configuration engine.

The foundational integration is already implemented
and tested. Do not redesign it.

GOAL:
Migrate all remaining public methods in one pass.

STRICT COMPATIBILITY:
- Keep the existing PropertiesManager class.
- Preserve every existing public method name,
  signature, return type and static modifier.
- Do not remove public methods.
- Existing consumer code must compile unchanged.
- Preserve legacy behavior when no active
  configuration binding exists.

IMPLEMENTATION:
1. Inspect all remaining public methods and
   their usages before changing them.

2. Route configuration reads through the
   active context's resolved snapshot.

3. Route configuration writes through the
   appropriate existing configuration updater.

4. Preserve source precedence and scope
   inheritance.

5. Reuse the existing binding, resolver,
   coordinator and layer store.

6. Avoid duplicated configuration storage
   when the new engine is active.

7. Preserve existing method-specific semantics,
   including defaults, empty values, nulls
   and environment selection.

8. Do not silently promote inherited values
   into local overrides.

9. Handle reset and reload methods carefully.
   Do not destroy active contexts or parent
   configuration layers.

10. Do not change already migrated methods
    unless necessary to fix a demonstrated defect.

11. Do not modify production listeners,
    TestNG lifecycle integration or module
    dependencies.

12. Keep core independent of TestNG.

TESTING:
- Add parameterized tests for the remaining
  methods and their expected behavior.
- Test ROOT, SUITE, TEST, CLASS and INVOCATION.
- Test parallel execution and nested activations.
- Test source precedence, inheritance and
  legacy compatibility.
- Test invalid and released contexts.
- Run the full Maven reactor.

IMPORTANT:
If any method cannot preserve its previous
semantics under the new architecture, do not
invent behavior. Leave that method unchanged,
report the exact incompatibility, and continue
migrating the other methods.

DELIVERABLES:
- List of migrated methods.
- List of methods left unchanged and why.
- Compatibility differences.
- Exact test results.
- Minimal production changes.








